---
description: Merge completed task branches into main before starting the next branch.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Mainline branch handoff

- Create each new task branch from the current local `main`.
- Finish, verify, and commit the current branch, then merge it into local `main` yourself before moving to another branch or task. Prefer a fast-forward merge. Resolve conflicts and rerun relevant checks if a fast-forward is unavailable.
- Confirm `main` contains every task commit and has no uncommitted tracked changes before creating the next branch.
- Do not leave completed work only on a task branch. Only an explicit user-approved exception may defer the merge or permit a new branch from elsewhere.
- This rule does not authorize a push, pull, deployment, or other remote operation.
